From 80a1aeb95fa7f530a8aa0e53cc8a37d7ac987762 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:50:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Do not write predicates into a header-only SVE signal
 context.

On an SME-only AArch64 machine Linux emits a 16-byte SVE header with
vl=0, followed by the TPIDR2 context. The SIGUSR2 context restore path
writes P2 and P6 beyond that empty record, corrupting TPIDR2. The kernel
rejects rt_sigreturn, so even native wineboot fails before thread entry.

Require a nonzero vector length and enough recorded storage for the full
SVE register payload before initializing the FEX predicates. Leave the
header-only context intact. This does not change the FEX source.

Reproduced the rejected signal return in a standalone signal-context test
on T8132 (4K and 16K execution); the guarded version returns normally.
Native Wine/default-prefix validation follows in the experiment report.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_arm64.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_arm64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_arm64.c
index c18e650..dc11689 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_arm64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_arm64.c
@@ -1399,7 +1399,11 @@ static void usr2_handler( int signal, siginfo_t *siginfo, void *sigcontext )
             memcpy( fp->vregs, frame->v, sizeof(fp->vregs) );
         }
 
-        if (sve)
+        /* SME-only systems can supply a header-only SVE context with vl=0.
+         * There is no predicate storage in that record; writing past it would
+         * corrupt the following extension and make rt_sigreturn fail. */
+        if (sve && sve->vl &&
+            sve->head.size >= SVE_SIG_CONTEXT_SIZE( sve_vq_from_vl(sve->vl) ))
         {
             /* setup FEX SVE state */
             ULONG64 vq = sve_vq_from_vl(sve->vl);
-- 
